  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "If \\(\\lvert x-\\log y\\rvert=x+\\log y,\\) where \\(x\\) and \\(\\log y\\) are real, then:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(x=0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(y=1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(x=0\\) and \\(y=1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(x(y-1)=0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "None of these"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1972-p8.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If \\(x-\\log y\\ge0,\\) the equation gives \\(\\log y=0,\\) hence \\(y=1.\\) If \\(x-\\log y\\lt0,\\) it gives \\(x=0.\\) Therefore every solution satisfies either \\(x=0\\) or \\(y=1,\\) which is expressed by \\[ x(y-1)=0. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Separate the cases \\(x-\\log y\\ge0\\) and \\(x-\\log y\\lt0\\)",
        "One case forces \\(\\log y=0\\), while the other forces \\(x=0\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
